#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A field given under its current and its legacy name, as about 0.2 % of
# COD files do. In the first block both names agree, only spelled
# differently: a short and a full Hermann-Mauguin symbol for one setting,
# and the same operations in another order, case and notation. No
# conflict. In the second, F d -3 m (standard origin choice 2) and
# F d -3 m :1 name different settings: a conflict, and the current name
# is used.
# Hand-written test fixture for Materials Workbench (mw-crystal-io); the
# layout follows COD entries such as 1512717 and 2312012, no values are
# copied.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

data_same_setting
_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'P 21/n'
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M    'P 1 21/n 1'
_cell_length_a                    5.0
_cell_length_b                    6.0
_cell_length_c                    7.0
_cell_angle_alpha                 90
_cell_angle_beta                  95
_cell_angle_gamma                 90
loop_
_space_group_symop_operation_xyz
'x, y, z'
'-x+1/2, y+1/2, -z+1/2'
'-x, -y, -z'
'x+1/2, -y+1/2, z+1/2'
loop_
_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz
-X,-Y,-Z
+X,+Y,+Z
1/2-X,1/2+Y,1/2-Z
1/2+X,1/2-Y,1/2+Z
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
C1 C 0.1 0.2 0.3

data_other_origin
_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'F d -3 m'
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M    'F d -3 m :1'
_cell_length_a                    5.431
_cell_length_b                    5.431
_cell_length_c                    5.431
_cell_angle_alpha                 90
_cell_angle_beta                  90
_cell_angle_gamma                 90
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
Si1 Si 0.125 0.125 0.125
